WEBVTT

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:03.920
Detection engineering increasingly adopts software engineering practices.

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:08.313
Teams use version control, peer review, testing, documentation, change management,

00:00:08.313 --> 00:00:13.613
CI/CD workflows, and lifecycle processes to manage detection content more consistently.

00:00:13.613 --> 00:00:17.154
Detection-as-Code does not mean every organization needs the same toolchain.

00:00:17.154 --> 00:00:20.647
The core idea is that detections should be treated as controlled, reviewable,

00:00:20.647 --> 00:00:24.347
testable assets rather than informal edits made directly in a console.

00:00:24.347 --> 00:00:28.451
Testing helps teams validate detection behavior before deployment and after changes to

00:00:28.451 --> 00:00:29.808
data sources or platforms.

00:00:29.808 --> 00:00:34.026
Documentation helps analysts and engineers understand purpose, expected behavior,

00:00:34.026 --> 00:00:36.000
dependencies, and response guidance.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.635
Engineering practices also make detection programs easier to scale.

00:00:39.635 --> 00:00:43.744
As the number of detections grows, teams need consistent naming, ownership, metadata,

00:00:43.744 --> 00:00:47.394
review schedules, and release processes to keep the program maintainable.

00:00:47.394 --> 00:00:49.074
This approach supports safer change.

00:00:49.074 --> 00:00:51.813
When detection logic is reviewed, tested, and documented,

00:00:51.813 --> 00:00:55.573
teams are less likely to introduce avoidable noise, break existing coverage,

00:00:55.573 --> 00:00:59.413
or lose track of why a detection was created. It also makes onboarding easier.

00:00:59.413 --> 00:01:02.082
New analysts and engineers can read the detection history,

00:01:02.082 --> 00:01:03.712
understand the intended behavior,

00:01:03.712 --> 00:01:07.512
and see how detections connect to telemetry sources and response workflows.

00:01:07.512 --> 00:01:09.931
Engineering discipline also supports accountability.

00:01:09.931 --> 00:01:14.051
Teams can define owners, service expectations, release steps, rollback options,

00:01:14.051 --> 00:01:19.510
and review cadences so detection content is managed with the same care as other production

00:01:19.510 --> 00:01:19.520
capabilities.
